==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bikinilan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Fabulous Pasalan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the Cats from [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Tales of the Nekoluga]], this Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Due to Bikinilan Pasalan's low base DPS and highly inconsistent Surge spawn area it is not recommended to use this Cat as one's only damage dealer. Instead, it should be used in tandem with other Cats with faster attack rates to keep enemies off of it.

Bikinilan Pasalan's low damage per hit allows it to be stacked against many more enemies with [[Barrier]]s than other [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] with similar DPS, though the stages where this can actually be done and is worth your time are few and far between.

It is most effective to use Bikinilan Pasalan to ward off enemies with many knockbacks, like [[Rain D.]] and [[Mr. Puffington]], because the Surge Attack lasts very long and can knockback those kinds of enemies several times on its own. It can also form a wall that may stop several [[Brollow]]s.

It is advisable to refrain from using Bikinilan Pasalan to attack the enemy base, because its Surge Attacks may go behind the base, effectively hitting none of the enemies that spawn, plus its DPS against it will not be increased by the surge (unless the enemy base is animated), as non-animated bases are immune to it. However, it can be good to trigger a boss wave with Bikinilan Pasalan, as the Surge, if it appears in front of the base, will immediately deliver high damage to anything that spawns. The general idea, however, is to spawn it after the boss wave.

==='''True Form'''===
The only improvement that Fabulous Pasalan sees is an increase to Surge level. This does boost its effective DPS, though the damage is still concentrated wherever the surge lands with an unreliably large spawn area. Another benefit of the longer surge is that it effectively reduces the time between surge attacks. The extended duration of the Surge and increased number of individual hits does improve its existing niches mentioned above, but it gains no new usage while still retaining the weaknesses that plague the previous form. Therefore, Fabulous Pasalan is not a high-priority True Form to unlock.

